## Why This Is Asked

This question blends sliding-window technique with binary search to analyze a threshold problem, testing practical algorithm design and reasoning about complexity.

## Key Concepts

- Sliding window for fixed-length subarray sums
- Binary search over the answer space
- Time/space trade-offs and edge-case handling
- Practical optimizations (early exit, optional prefix sums)

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxLWithSumAtMost(A, T) {
  const n = A.length;
  const ok = (L) => {
    let sum = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < L; i++) sum += A[i];
    if (sum <= T) return true;
    for (let i = L; i < n; i++) {
      sum += A[i] - A[i - L];
      if (sum <= T) return true;
    }
    return false;
  };
  let lo = 1, hi = n, ans = 0;
  while (lo <= hi) {
    const mid = (lo + hi) >> 1;
    if (ok(mid)) { ans = mid; lo = mid + 1; } else { hi = mid - 1; }
  }
  return ans;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would the solution change if elements could be negative?
- What are the memory/speed trade-offs if you precompute prefix sums?
- How would you adapt for multiple thresholds T1..Tk in parallel?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical amortized analysis for dynamic frequency tracking, demonstrates how to monitor hot keys efficiently, and contrasts incremental updates with full recomputation.

## Key Concepts
- Amortized analysis for batched updates
- Frequency buckets for O(1) max-frequency queries
- Hash maps for per-label counts
- Sparse vs. dense label domains
- Space-time tradeoff analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
class HotKeyTracker {
  constructor(initialCounts) {
    this.cnt = new Map();
    this.freq = new Map();
    this.maxFreq = 0;
    for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(initialCounts)) {
      this.cnt.set(k, v);
      this.freq.set(v, (this.freq.get(v) || 0) + 1);
      this.maxFreq = Math.max(this.maxFreq, v);
    }
  }

  update(label, delta) {
    const old = this.cnt.get(label) || 0;
    const freqCount = this.freq.get(old) || 0;
    if (freqCount === 1) this.freq.delete(old);
    else this.freq.set(old, freqCount - 1);

    const nw = old + delta;
    this.cnt.set(label, nw);
    this.freq.set(nw, (this.freq.get(nw) || 0) + 1);
    this.maxFreq = Math.max(this.maxFreq, nw);
  }

  hasHotKey(threshold) {
    return this.maxFreq >= threshold;
  }
}
```

