## Key Concepts
- Incremental triangle counting; degree-based orientation; amortized analysis; sparse graphs; memory efficiency.

## Code Example
```javascript
function addBatch(G, batch){
  // G stores oriented adj lists and degree
  for(const [u,v] of batch){
    if(G.deg[u] > G.deg[v] || (G.deg[u] === G.deg[v] && u > v)) swap(u,v);
    // ensure oriented edge u->v
    G.adj[u].push(v);
    const common = intersect(G.adj[u], G.out[v]);
    G.triangles += common.length;
  }
}
```

